MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Eagles: The Very Best Of feels like a natural choice because its melodic guitars and relaxed country-rock sound connect with the blues and roots-oriented music I have been choosing.",
    "Led Zeppelin IV, Abbey Road, and The Beatles 1 capture parts of my interest in blues-based guitar playing and melodic rock, even though I would only choose the Eagles collection today."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Fallen, American Idiot, and St. Anger share a broad rock connection with my listening, but their heavier or more aggressive sounds miss the relaxed, roots-oriented feel I want now.",
    "Adele's albums and Partners emphasize pop vocals or duets rather than the guitar-led blues and rock that currently interest me, so I would pass on them."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The choices seem to treat an interest in rock as a reason to offer everything from melodic classic rock to punk and metal, although those sounds serve very different moods for me.",
    "Several choices feel based on broadly familiar albums, but familiarity alone gives me little reason to choose something today."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The connection across my recent choices is more about blues influence, roots-oriented songwriting, and guitar playing than simply belonging to rock.",
    "My preference today is for a mellower, melodic sound: I can appreciate Led Zeppelin or the Beatles while still feeling that the Eagles are the only choice worth acting on this visit."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly recognize my interest in guitar-led rock but stretch it too broadly and miss my current preference for relaxed blues and roots-oriented music."
}
